[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Companion & Romance Roadmap[/b] is a live, in-game checklist for every companion's personal quest and romance, read straight from your save.

Most of what matters for a companion is easy to miss: a conversation you never had, a long rest you skipped, an area you can never go back to. Wikis tell you what [i]can[/i] happen. This mod tells you, inside the game, what has already happened in your playthrough and what is still open.

Press [b]F7[/b] and pick a companion:
[list]
[*][b]Where you stand[/b]: recruited, dating, partnered or lost, with live approval and its tier.
[*][b]What to do next[/b]: every step of their quest and romance, act by act. Where to go, what to do, what to avoid, rewards, and the approval each step needs next to yours. The next step is highlighted.
[*][b]What you are about to lose[/b]: the [i]Before you move on[/i] tab lists every upcoming point of no return and what is still open before it.
[/list]
Steps tick themselves off as you play. Everything is read from the game's own journal, story flags and approval values, so nothing is guessed, and the mod never changes your game.

[b][color=#e0a45c]Work in progress:[/color][/b] this is an early release. The guide and its detection keep improving with every update, and you may run into bugs or steps that are not detected yet. Some moments only exist inside a conversation and leave no trace in the save; those show as [i]Not seen[/i] and you can check them off by hand. Please report anything wrong on the Bugs tab or on [url=https://github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/CompanionRoadmap/issues/new/choose]GitHub[/url]. The report file helps most: in the roadmap window choose [b]Options > Create a report file[/b], then attach it on GitHub or paste its contents.

[b]New in 1.0.2:[/b] every companion's page now opens with the choices that lose them for good (71 golden rules in all, the new ones checked against the game's own story scripts), a companion the game has removed is shown as lost even when the journal says nothing, and both known issues of 1.0.1 are fixed. What was reviewed is listed on [url=https://github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/CompanionRoadmap/blob/main/docs/COVERAGE.md]GitHub[/url] (spoilers).

Open source (MIT): [url=https://github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/CompanionRoadmap]github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/CompanionRoadmap[/url][/color][/size]

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8][list=1]
[*]Install the [url=https://github.com/Norbyte/bg3se/releases]BG3 Script Extender[/url] if you have not already.
[*]Install this mod with your mod manager:
[list]
[*][b]BG3 Mod Manager[/b]: import the zip, move [i]Companion & Romance Roadmap[/i] to the active list, then save and export the load order.
[*][b]Vortex[/b]: install, enable, deploy.
[*][b]Manual[/b]: put [i]CompanionRoadmap.pak[/i] in [i]%LOCALAPPDATA%\Larian Studios\Baldur's Gate 3\Mods[/i] and enable it in your mod manager.
[/list]
[*]Load a save and press [b]F7[/b]. With Mod Configuration Menu installed you can also open it from the mod's MCM page.
[/list]
It is safe to add in the middle of a playthrough: the roadmap reads what the game has already recorded.
To uninstall, disable or remove it. Saves made with it still load; the game only warns that a mod is missing.[/color][/size]

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8][list]
[*]All [b]10 recruitable companions[/b] and around [b]100 steps[/b]: Shadowheart, Minthara, Karlach, Lae'zel, Astarion, Gale, Wyll, Halsin, Jaheira and Minsc.
[*][b]Golden rules[/b] on every page: the choices that make that companion die or leave for good, plus a short list that applies to all of them. They follow your spoiler setting.
[*][b]Live statuses[/b] (Next, To do, Optional, Not seen, Waiting, Later, Done, Checked, Missed, N/A), updated within half a second. Hover a status to see what it means.
[*][b]Points of no return[/b]: entering the Shadowfell (Act 1 locks), the Mind Flayer Colony, leaving for Baldur's Gate, the Lower City and the final battle, each with what you would still lose. Click an entry to jump to that step.
[*][b]Hidden trackers[/b]: Shadowheart's Nightsong points (4 of 6 make sparing Nightsong far easier), Karlach's engine upgrades and the magic items fed to Gale.
[*][b]The easy-to-miss details[/b]: Shadowheart's wolf memory (needed for the Act 3 swim), Minthara's non-lethal knockout rules, Karlach's Act 2 night, Gale's starry night before the Colony, Wyll's party-only romance start, Astarion's ascension checks, and more.
[*][b]Notifications[/b] when a romance or important step is completed or missed.
[*][b]Manual check-offs[/b] for moments the game does not record or another mod changes. They are saved in your savegame.
[*][b]Spoiler control[/b]: the roadmap asks once how much it may reveal about later acts (everything, step titles only, or nothing). Until you choose, later acts stay hidden.
[*][b]Companion portraits[/b] from the game's own Photo Mode stickers (can be switched off).
[*][b]One-click report file[/b] for bug reports: it lists what the tracker sees in your save, game identifiers only.
[*][b]Looks like it belongs in BG3[/b]: a quiet dark panel in the game's own Quadraat typeface, with colour only where it means something.
[*][b]Mod Configuration Menu[/b] support: a settings page, a rebindable hotkey and an [i]Open roadmap[/i] button. Without MCM, every option is in the window's Options tab.
[*][b]Multiplayer and origin aware[/b]: each player sees their own approval and romance, and playing as an origin marks that companion's recruitment and romance as not applicable.
[*][b]Plays nicely with other mods[/b]: romance mods such as PolyamoryFixes and NoRomanceLimit work (check a step off by hand if a mod changes how it is recorded). Mods that rewrite a companion's story, such as Really Shadowheart, should still be detected, but the guide describes the unmodded game; details on GitHub. The mod is read-only: it never changes flags, approval, quests or items.
[*]Default key [b]F7[/b]. F8 is deliberately avoided because it is the game's Quickload.
[/list][/color][/size]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8][list]
[*][url=https://github.com/Norbyte/bg3se/releases]BG3 Script Extender[/url]: [b]required[/b], v25 or newer.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/baldursgate3/mods/9162]Mod Configuration Menu[/url]: optional, for a settings page, a rebindable hotkey and an Open roadmap button.
[*]Baldur's Gate 3 Patch 8. The guide data is verified against the Patch 8 Hotfix 10 game files.
[/list]
The roadmap's text is in English only for now.[/color][/size]

